  "description": {
    "text": "Battle Road Spring 2002 held nine tournaments at seven venues, from Tokyo on 9 March to Sapporo on 7 April 2002. It was the first year Japan's regional circuit was open to all ages, with a new masters league for players 16 and over beside the junior and senior ones. The top three of each league won No. 1, 2 or 3 Trainer, Ken Sugimori's trainer art in the e-Card frame in a boy's and a girl's version, printed with the winner's name, tournament, league and place, with a message from Imakuni? in its e-Reader dot code. Winners were handed a dark blue folio and certificate on stage, and the cards were mailed to them in May 2002. The winners' lists in Trainers magazine show few girls among them, which makes the girl's versions the rarer.",
